-- SYNTAX -------------------- errors/parse_error_9.march

A `let?` binding can't have a type annotation — its type is inferred from the `Ok` payload of the `Result` on the right. [parse_error]

8 |     let? x : Int = get()
               ^

    let? name = result_expr
    After this is fixed, `main` will also need permission to print: add `needs IO.Console` to the module, and give `main` the grant, `fn main(_console : Cap(IO.Console))`.
    run `march --explain parse_error`
